# Wendigo

**Alignments.** Any, but most are good: gentle, compassionate and caring.

Also known as Sasquatch and Big Foot. Seven to eight feet tall and 250 to 400
pounds, the Wendigo keep to the deep wilderness and are almost never seen, but
they watch anyone who comes near their territories. Harmless woodsmen and
hunters are left alone and sometimes helped in hard times; despoilers,
trophy-hunters and armed bands are watched, lured away, driven off - and killed
if they prove a real danger to the Wendigo, their sacred sites or the innocent.
Evil supernatural beings are chased away or destroyed.

## Lore

Printed 126-127 casts the Wendigo as guardians of the forest who keep quiet
tabs on humankind through the woodsmen they befriend. Player characters take one
of the Native American O.C.C.s, or one of four simpler occupations with half
their usual related skills.
', 'published', 'data-script'
